<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conrad of Montferrat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1146–<a href="/years/1192">1192</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conrad of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> was an Italian nobleman who arrived at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a> in 1187 and held it against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. He became Marquis of Montferrat and, through marriage to Isabella, claimant to the crown of Jerusalem, and was elected king in April 1192. Days later he was murdered in Tyre by two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismailism">Nizari</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassins</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-of-montferrat.jpg" alt="Conrad of Montferrat" width="320" height="571" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IsabelaKOnrad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Defeat at Hattin in 1187 cost it almost all its territory, though Tyre held out under <b>Conrad of Montferrat</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Conrad of Montferrat</b>, who had held Tyre against Saladin after the fall of Jerusalem, was murdered in the city by two Nizari Assassins.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-28">28 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Conrad of Montferrat</b>, who had held Tyre against Saladin, married Isabella I of Jerusalem and so became de facto King of Jerusalem.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/november-24">24 November in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1187, when Saladin's victory left almost every other town lost, <b>Conrad of Montferrat</b> arrived and held Tyre against him, ruling it as his own base.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-tyre">Lordship of Tyre</a></li><li><blockquote>The Aleramici were famed crusaders: <b>Conrad of Montferrat</b> defended Tyre and was elected King of Jerusalem in 1192, and Boniface I led the Fourth Crusade and became King of Thessalonica.</blockquote><a href="/state/march-of-montferrat">March of Montferrat</a></li><li><blockquote>The Nizaris used targeted killings by devotees against powerful enemies, including <b>Conrad of Montferrat</b> in 1192, and twice attempted to kill Saladin.</blockquote><a href="/state/nizari-ismailis-of-syria">Nizari Ismailis of Syria</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casale-monferrato">Casale Monferrato</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Tyre, in what is now <a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.13,8.46&amp;year=1175" aria-label="Casale Monferrato on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4751 570 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Conrad of Montferrat"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5201 840h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5201 840h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.13,8.46&amp;year=1175">What was here in 1175? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
